WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Finding food help in Alabama's Black Belt
shouldn't be this hard.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.040
Picture a mom in Wilcox County
with two kids and no time to waste.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.000
She needs a pantry that's close,
and open today.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.600
AccessBelt maps 883 food pantries
across 67 Alabama counties.

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.200
She picks her county,
sees the closest pantry,

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.440
and gets directions,
or calls ahead with one tap.

7
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.280
Every pin tells you what we know.

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.080
Orange pantries have current contact info.

9
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.000
Grey ones aren't verified yet,
so the app reminds you to call ahead.

10
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.720
Now picture a grandfather
who doesn't do apps.

11
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.600
He just asks Pete: “Pantries near me.”

12
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.120
Pete answers in plain words
and even tells him what to bring.

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.960
A photo ID, proof of address, and a bag.

14
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.400
For families stretching every dollar,
SNAP and WIC help is one tap away.

15
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.280
And if tonight is a crisis, call 211.
Free, 24/7.

16
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.720
AccessBelt is free, private,
and there's no account to make.

17
00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.540
Help is closer than you think.

18
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.050
Get AccessBelt, free on the App Store.
